00:06:50.000 --> 00:07:23.000
We cannot burn our dead because that's polluting fire, and fire is seen as the Son of God. So Zoroastrians have always had this unusual method of giving back to nature. By giving back to nature, what Kogeste means is that after priests have said their final prayers, the corpse bearers will place a body atop one of these towers. Then they will wait for the vultures to come. Rashne Bardiwala grew up in a Parsi family,

