to shoot vultures around airports because they posed such a hazard to air traffic. You know, they were just always there. They were always there and there were so many of them. In this story, we're mostly referring to a genus of vultures called gyps vultures. And these birds, they just have this look about them. The look, you know, not the best. I won't say ugly, but they don't look very attractive as a bird.

