I hope you're not in a hurry," he said. I had time, but I didn't exactly have space. The room Aspi and I were in was full of Parsi elders, and there was nothing I could say to convince them to leave, especially since it's unusual for Kandiyas to speak publicly like this. I grew up around several nosy Indian aunties, though, not to mention I live in fear of becoming one. So I get it. With a little coaxing, I got each uncle to please mute their WhatsApp notifications.

